// # Opm QA Index — Anchor for Agents
//
// Logline: Index of the 8 break-test drivers that ship with opm.
//
// Setup: Each proof driver is a hostile test for one shipped function. If a driver fails, opm fails to release.
//
// Beats:
//   1. today_proof.oo — proves the today-claim signer passes bit-identical double-run.
//   2. tomorrow_proof.oo — proves the tomorrow-revoke gate is fail-closed.
//   3. extract_proof.oo — proves archive extraction refuses traversal.
//   4. ingest_proof.oo — proves registry ingest rejects malformed manifests.
//   5. init_proof.oo — proves project init lays down the XDG tree correctly.
//   6. lock_format_proof.oo — proves the lockfile format is round-trip stable.
//   7. pubgrub_proof.oo — proves the resolver terminates and returns valid plans.
//   8. semver_proof.oo — proves the SemVer parser handles edge cases.

import "today_proof.oo";
import "tomorrow_proof.oo";
import "extract_proof.oo";
import "ingest_proof.oo";
import "init_proof.oo";
import "lock_format_proof.oo";
import "pubgrub_proof.oo";
import "semver_proof.oo";
